---
/* A link, not a button: the design allows no buttons, and a jump to `#top` is
   navigation anyway. `scroll-behavior: smooth` on `html` already carries the
   travel, and it is declared under `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, so
   a reader who asked for less motion gets an instant jump for free. */
---

<div class="to-top-rail" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <a class="to-top" href="#top" aria-label="Back to top" title="Back to top">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <path d="M12 19.5v-15" />
      <path d="M5.5 11L12 4.5 18.5 11" />
    </svg>
  </a>
</div>

<style>
  /* The reveal, with no script.

     Two moving parts, and both are load-bearing. The rail is out of flow and
     starts one viewport down, which caps how far the anchor can be lifted: a
     sticky element may not be shifted outside its containing block. The anchor
     sits at the rail's far end, because `bottom` only ever shifts an element
     upward, so an anchor starting at the rail's top would have nothing to hold
     and would simply scroll away.

     Together they put the anchor's clamped position at one viewport plus its own
     height, just under the fold, wherever the document ends. It surfaces after
     roughly 40px of scrolling and then stays pinned, on a short page and a long
     one alike.

     Two alternatives were rejected. `animation-timeline: scroll()` reads better
     but stable Firefox does not implement it, which would leave the anchor
     permanently visible there. A scroll listener would be a fourth inline
     script, and `npm run audit:dist` asserts three. */
  .to-top-rail {
    position: absolute;
    top: 100vh;
    bottom: 0;
    right: var(--page-gutter);
    width: 2.5rem;
    /* Above the frosted page panel, which sits at z-index 2. */
    z-index: 3;
    /* The rail spans nearly the whole document, so it must never swallow a
       click meant for the text underneath it. */
    pointer-events: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
  }

  .to-top {
    position: sticky;
    bottom: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    /* Same frosted treatment as the header and the page panel, because over the
       grove a bare icon has nothing to hold it. */
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-blur));
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-light);
    display: flex;
    height: 2.5rem;
    justify-content: center;
    pointer-events: auto;
    transition: color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
    width: 2.5rem;
  }

  .to-top:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink-deep);
  }
</style>
